    {
      "id": "slope-and-forms",
      "title": "Slope and forms of a line",
      "notes": "The **slope** of the line through $(x_1, y_1)$ and $(x_2, y_2)$ is\n$$m = \\frac{y_2 - y_1}{x_2 - x_1} = \\tan\\theta$$\n\n- Parallel lines: $m_1 = m_2$. Perpendicular lines: $m_1 m_2 = -1$.\n\n**Forms of the equation**\n\n| Form | Equation |\n|---|---|\n| Point–slope | $y - y_1 = m(x - x_1)$ |\n| Slope–intercept | $y = mx + c$ |\n| Intercept | $\\dfrac{x}{a} + \\dfrac{y}{b} = 1$ |\n| General | $Ax + By + C = 0$, slope $-\\dfrac{A}{B}$ |",
      "widget": {
        "module": "graph",
        "label": "Slope m and intercept c",
        "params": {
          "e1": "y = m x + c",
          "e2": "m = 1",
          "e3": "c = 2",
          "e4": "(0, c)",
          "e5": "y = -x/m + c"
        }
      },
      "examples": [
        {
          "problem": "Find the line through $(2, 3)$ perpendicular to $y = 2x + 1$.",
          "solution": "Slope $-\\tfrac12$: $y - 3 = -\\tfrac12(x - 2)$, i.e. $x + 2y - 8 = 0$."
        }
      ],
      "quiz": [
        {
          "id": "s1",
          "type": "numeric",
          "prompt": "Slope of the line through (1, 2) and (3, 8)?",
          "answer": 3,
          "hint": "",
          "explanation": "",
          "tolerance": 0.01
        },
        {
